amount of any cash and the fair market value of any other property received upon the sale,
exchange, or other taxable disposition of the shares. A U.S. Holder’s tax basis in a share generally
will be equal to the cost of the share to such U.S. Holder, which may be adjusted for certain
subsequent events (for example, if the U.S. Holder receives a nondividend distribution, as described
