stock, preferred stock, or depositary shares generally will be capital gain or loss and will be long-
term capital gain or loss if the shares have been held for more than one year. Net long-term capital
gain recognized by an individual U.S. Holder is generally taxed at preferential rates. The ability of
U.S. Holders to deduct capital losses is subject to limitations under the Code.
